- Mouth off!

250
00:19:57.986 --> 00:20:00.648
- Hey. everyone's a critic.
- Hello?

251
00:20:00.610 --> 00:20:02.874
Oh. man!

252
00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:06.479
- April. you spoiled our surprise.
- We were gonna clean everything up.

253
00:20:06.401 --> 00:20:09.700
Thanks. guys.
Where's Splinter?

254
00:20:10.305 --> 00:20:13.365
He's been up on the roof
ever since he saw your report.

255
00:20:14.241 --> 00:20:16.539
Really? Doing what?

256
00:20:16.513 --> 00:20:20.005
Coming to a decision.

257
00:20:21.025 --> 00:20:24.017
You've been meditating many hours.
Master Splinter.

258
00:20:23.969 --> 00:20:28.269
Yes. and it is time.
join me above.

259
00:20:29.280 --> 00:20:31.805
Maybe you better hear
what he has to say.

260
00:20:31.776 --> 00:20:35.940
These last hours
have been spent...

261
00:20:35.841 --> 00:20:39.436
pondering many questions.

262
00:20:39.360 --> 00:20:44.889
Some are the very questions
of our origin.

263
00:20:44.736 --> 00:20:46.135
The sewer.

264
00:20:46.144 --> 00:20:48.840
Our transformation.

265
00:20:48.799 --> 00:20:52.030
But the answers have
always remained...

266
00:20:51.967 --> 00:20:54.731
hidden in the past...

267
00:20:54.688 --> 00:20:59.250
veiled by a shadow
too deep to penetrate...

268
00:21:00.511 --> 00:21:01.842
until now.

269
00:21:04.703 --> 00:21:07.069
A light from the present...

270
00:21:07.039 --> 00:21:11.772
reaches back
to illuminate that shadow.

271
00:21:11.647 --> 00:21:15.879
You have never seen this.
but know what it is.

272
00:21:16.415 --> 00:21:21.352
- That's the canister that had the ooze!
- That transformed us all.

273
00:21:21.215 --> 00:21:25.151
i have kept it these 15 years.

274
00:21:25.054 --> 00:21:28.683
But why do you only show us
now. Master Splinter?

275
00:21:31.933 --> 00:21:34.026
TGRi!

276
00:21:34.013 --> 00:21:37.005
The interview today.
i knew it!

277
00:21:36.957 --> 00:21:39.983
i knew that there was something else
going on with those guys.

278
00:21:39.933 --> 00:21:43.425
Yes. and we must know what...

279
00:21:43.357 --> 00:21:47.350
for if the contents of this
canister were not unique...

280
00:21:47.261 --> 00:21:51.994
the city may now face
grave danger.

281
00:21:51.869 --> 00:21:54.667
After all these years.

282
00:21:54.620 --> 00:21:57.589
After all this time
wondering who we are.

283
00:21:57.533 --> 00:22:02.027
The past returns. my son.

284
00:22:03.676 --> 00:22:09.114
it is time to seek our answers.

285
00:22:41.402 --> 00:22:43.393
Disposed.

286
00:22:48.314 --> 00:22:51.340
Well. you're the last one.
aren't you?

287
00:22:57.082 --> 00:22:59.778
- Come on guys.
- I love this spy stuff.

288
00:22:59.738 --> 00:23:01.672
Yeah.

289
00:23:05.753 --> 00:23:07.687
Not much to this place.

290
00:23:09.465 --> 00:23:11.456
it doesn't look like
there's any night security...

291
00:23:11.449 --> 00:23:13.542
but we better
move in quiet.

292
00:23:13.529 --> 00:23:15.827
- Yeah.
- Come on. Leo.

293
00:23:15.801 --> 00:23:19.897
What do you say?
Let's do it. eh?

294
00:23:19.800 --> 00:23:22.633
- Let's do it!
- Let's do it!

295
00:23:23.864 --> 00:23:26.355
- Times Square city!
- I don't believe it!

296
00:23:26.328 --> 00:23:29.923
- Like video games in 3-D!
- Totally massive!

297
00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:33.798
Would you get a load
of this crazy joint!

298
00:23:33.752 --> 00:23:37.688
The past returns. I knew
we'd find something special.

299
00:23:37.591 --> 00:23:40.151
i'll say special.
Look at this.

300
00:23:40.119 --> 00:23:44.453
- Hey. where do you put the quarter?
- Will you stop messing around?

301
00:23:44.344 --> 00:23:46.642
Hey. guys. over there!

302
00:23:53.879 --> 00:23:56.677
- What do you make of it. Donny?
- Well. i'm not sure.

303
00:23:56.630 --> 00:23:58.564
Looks like just a bunch
of serial numbers.

304
00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:00.347
Let's see. uh...

305
00:24:00.343 --> 00:24:03.312
Disposed.
Disposed.

306
00:24:04.151 --> 00:24:07.678
- Disposed.
- Hey. dudes. we're too late.

307
00:24:07.606 --> 00:24:10.166
Like. uh. no deposit.
no return.

308
00:24:10.134 --> 00:24:12.762
Well. except maybe this one.

309
00:24:12.726 --> 00:24:14.785
What do you mean?

310
00:24:14.774 --> 00:24:15.968
Look!

311
00:24:17.206 --> 00:24:18.138
"Active."

312
00:24:18.166 --> 00:24:20.327
- Yeah.
- Can you bring up the file?

313
00:24:20.310 --> 00:24:23.108
Well. i could try.

314
00:24:23.061 --> 00:24:26.724
But if the database is coded.
the whole system might go down.

315
00:24:28.437 --> 00:24:30.928
- Do it!
- Yeah. yeah!

316
00:24:42.581 --> 00:24:44.071
- Drag.
- Drat.

317
00:24:44.084 --> 00:24:47.281
No. no. no! So close!

318
00:24:50.581 --> 00:24:53.709
- What?
- The Foot!

319
00:24:56.052 --> 00:24:57.781
He's got the canister!

320
00:24:57.780 --> 00:25:00.180
- Get it!
- I got him!

321
00:25:17.683 --> 00:25:18.672
Go. go. go. go!

322
00:25:38.227 --> 00:25:40.991
- Throw it over here.
- Go long! Go long!

323
00:25:40.946 --> 00:25:43.506
Down field!
Turtle in the open!

324
00:25:47.602 --> 00:25:50.298
Ah. one. two. three. punt!

325
00:25:56.177 --> 00:25:59.010
Hey. guys. huddle.
Come here. Come on.

326
00:25:58.961 --> 00:26:01.896
Mikey. you go up the middle.
You guys take the sides.

327
00:26:01.841 --> 00:26:05.140
- Got it.
- I don't get it.

328
00:26:05.073 --> 00:26:06.233
Ready. break!

329
00:26:28.464 --> 00:26:31.262
Hey. Mikey. surf's up. dude!

330
00:26:34.063 --> 00:26:35.928
Wipe out!

331
00:26:39.119 --> 00:26:41.178
Ninja vanish!

332
00:26:48.527 --> 00:26:50.518
Oh. great!

333
00:26:52.206 --> 00:26:54.538
Terrific!

334
00:26:56.398 --> 00:26:58.389
Wonderful!

335
00:27:02.318 --> 00:27:04.309
Bummer!

336
00:27:06.926 --> 00:27:10.987
And this was the only one?

337
00:27:10.893 --> 00:27:13.191
Then it's time to
find out exactly...

338
00:27:13.166 --> 00:27:17.296
what this ooze can do.

339
00:27:17.198 --> 00:27:20.190
isn't it. Professor?

340
00:27:22.189 --> 00:27:25.283
We'll find a home soon. Paulina.
and then it'll be just you and me.

341
00:27:25.229 --> 00:27:28.596
Now. look. we've all talked about it.
We've decided to do it...

342
00:27:28.525 --> 00:27:31.426
- And that's all there is to it.
- But i don't understand.

343
00:27:31.373 --> 00:27:33.933
You guys haven't even found
a new place to live yet.

344
00:27:33.901 --> 00:27:38.201
it's too dangerous to stay here with you
when the Foot are out there.

345
00:27:38.092 --> 00:27:40.060
They might be looking for us.

346
00:27:40.045 --> 00:27:42.809
We could go looking for them
for a change.

347
00:27:42.765 --> 00:27:44.790
i mean. they've got the ooze.

348
00:27:44.780 --> 00:27:48.477
- First we move. then we look.
- I don't know about you guys...

349
00:27:48.396 --> 00:27:52.127
- But i could really go for a slice of...
- Pizza!

350
00:27:52.044 --> 00:27:53.477
Whoa! Spookular!

351
00:27:53.484 --> 00:27:55.748
Miss O'Neil?

352
00:27:58.539 --> 00:28:02.566
Wait! I'll be right there.

353
00:28:07.435 --> 00:28:11.303
- What?
- I didn't order any pizza.

354
00:28:11.211 --> 00:28:14.476
Oh. i know.
But the guy in 313 did...

355
00:28:14.411 --> 00:28:16.879
and now he doesn't
seem to be there.

356
00:28:17.898 --> 00:28:20.332
i figured since you
order so much anyway...

357
00:28:20.299 --> 00:28:22.859
that. you know. maybe you...

358
00:28:24.587 --> 00:28:27.522
- Where'd these come from?
- Those...

359
00:28:27.466 --> 00:28:29.127
are mine!

360
00:28:29.130 --> 00:28:31.189
Yeah. I...

361
00:28:31.178 --> 00:28:35.205
i like to do a little chucking
every now and then.

362
00:28:40.073 --> 00:28:43.236
Yeah.
i'd keep practicing.

363
00:28:43.178 --> 00:28:46.614
On second thought.
why don't i take this pizza anyway?

364
00:28:46.537 --> 00:28:49.404
i can always use more.
Let me get my wallet.

365
00:28:49.354 --> 00:28:50.787
No. that's okay.

366
00:28:50.793 --> 00:28:52.727
- Yes. please.
- Don't worry about it.

367
00:28:52.713 --> 00:28:55.307
One last thing. though.
You might want to know about this!

368
00:28:56.681 --> 00:28:59.149
- You guys!
- What's the big idea?

369
00:28:59.113 --> 00:29:02.708
Can i hurt him? Please!
Tell me i can hurt him!

370
00:29:02.633 --> 00:29:04.760
- Please. please!
- Take it easy.

371
00:29:08.297 --> 00:29:12.063
i think you'd better sit down.

372
00:29:19.400 --> 00:29:23.131
And with an old
Renaissance art book...

373
00:29:23.048 --> 00:29:25.915
i found in a storm drain...

374
00:29:25.864 --> 00:29:28.298
i gave them all names.

375
00:29:28.264 --> 00:29:30.357
Yeah.

376
00:29:30.343 --> 00:29:33.938
i'm Leonardo.

377
00:29:33.863 --> 00:29:35.956
i'm Michaelangelo.

378
00:29:37.351 --> 00:29:39.285
Donatello.

379
00:29:39.271 --> 00:29:41.205
i'm Rafael.

380
00:29:41.191 --> 00:29:43.921
Yeah. all the good ones
end in "O."

381
00:29:45.862 --> 00:29:48.023
- Michaelangelo!
- Yeah?

382
00:29:48.007 --> 00:29:51.101
- Go!
- All right.

383
00:29:51.047 --> 00:29:54.380
i can't believe
every time i...

384
00:29:56.359 --> 00:29:57.724
One.

385
00:29:59.846 --> 00:30:02.280
- Two.
- Basically. what you're telling me...

386
00:30:02.246 --> 00:30:05.306
is you guys were all slimed!

387
00:30:06.021 --> 00:30:10.583
it wasn't slime. It was ooze.
And there's more of it out there.

388
00:30:10.469 --> 00:30:12.801
- Where?
- We're not sure.

389
00:30:12.774 --> 00:30:15.538
See. there's this sort of
clan of ninja thieves.

390
00:30:15.493 --> 00:30:17.791
- A secret group. They call themselves...
- The Foot?

391
00:30:17.765 --> 00:30:20.325
- You've heard of'em?
- The word is out...

392
00:30:20.293 --> 00:30:23.353
that these guys are looking
for anybody they can find...

393
00:30:23.301 --> 00:30:26.327
with martial arts talent.
especially teenagers.

394
00:30:27.173 --> 00:30:33.009
Hey. and if i let myself get recruited.
guess what that might lead us to?

395
00:30:32.837 --> 00:30:35.032
No way. Keno.

396
00:30:35.012 --> 00:30:37.276
Forget about it.

397
00:30:37.252 --> 00:30:40.915
Believe me. i really hate to say this.
but the kid's got a...

398
00:30:40.836 --> 00:30:43.327
- No!
- Why not?

399
00:30:43.300 --> 00:30:46.360
Too dangerous.

400
00:30:46.308 --> 00:30:47.741
But i thought we...

401
00:30:49.956 --> 00:30:50.888
Oh. man.

402
00:30:50.916 --> 00:30:53.544
Twenty.

403
00:30:53.507 --> 00:30:56.499
Twenty-one.
Twenty...

404
00:31:00.676 --> 00:31:02.769
One? Yeah.

405
00:31:09.379 --> 00:31:12.871
And these are the two most vicious
animals you could find?

406
00:31:13.762 --> 00:31:15.730
Good.

407
00:31:15.715 --> 00:31:18.411
- Professor?
- Preparations are complete. however...

408
00:31:18.370 --> 00:31:21.635
- Begin!
- I must re-register my protest...

409
00:31:21.570 --> 00:31:23.697
and remind you
of the immense danger if...

410
00:31:26.978 --> 00:31:30.209
That's enough talk from me.
We'll begin.

411
00:32:00.385 --> 00:32:02.979
Yes.

412
00:32:08.864 --> 00:32:11.458
- Clear.
- Go. go. Move.

413
00:32:18.464 --> 00:32:20.455
- See ya. April.
- Bye.

414
00:32:22.976 --> 00:32:24.204
Wish us luck.

415
00:32:28.767 --> 00:32:30.758
We'll be back for Splinter.

416
00:32:32.607 --> 00:32:36.475
The lives of two people don't amount
to a hill of beans in this crazy world.

417
00:32:36.383 --> 00:32:38.317
That's why you're
gettin' on that plane.

418
00:32:38.302 --> 00:32:40.668
- Maybe not today. maybe not to...
- Would you stop!

419
00:32:41.726 --> 00:32:43.057
See ya.

420
00:33:00.062 --> 00:33:03.225
All right. hold it.
This is stupid.

421
00:33:03.165 --> 00:33:05.156
We got the Foot up there
with the ooze...

422
00:33:05.150 --> 00:33:07.584
and we're down here
playing "Century 21."

423
00:33:07.549 --> 00:33:09.813
- Raph!
- Come on. Leo.

424
00:33:09.789 --> 00:33:12.383
Even you could think of something
better to do than this.

425
00:33:12.349 --> 00:33:15.341
i already have.
Now. let's get going!

426
00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:17.591
That's it.
i'm goin' up.

427
00:33:18.108 --> 00:33:21.544
- No. you're not!
- Let go of my arm. Leo.

428
00:33:21.469 --> 00:33:25.337
Guys. guys. guys!
i just got an idea.

429
00:33:25.244 --> 00:33:28.270
Two words that could solve
all our housing problems.

430
00:33:28.220 --> 00:33:31.485
Time share!

431
00:33:31.420 --> 00:33:34.412
- Not quite ripe yet.
- I'm outta here.

432
00:33:34.364 --> 00:33:37.060
But... Oh. man!

433
00:33:37.755 --> 00:33:40.223
Oh. boy.

434
00:33:41.403 --> 00:33:43.371
- Come on.
- Yeah.

435
00:33:43.356 --> 00:33:48.259
- Finding a home should be easy.
- But no!

436
00:33:48.123 --> 00:33:50.387
You'd think even an idiot
could find a place down here.

437
00:33:50.363 --> 00:33:51.887
But no...

438
00:33:53.883 --> 00:33:56.408
Oh. no!
Mikey. buddy!

439
00:33:56.379 --> 00:33:59.576
- Mikey. are you okay?
- Mikey!

440
00:33:59.515 --> 00:34:02.484
Check it out!

441
00:34:02.427 --> 00:34:03.792
Yeah!

442
00:34:03.803 --> 00:34:07.762
- Whoa!
- Okay. bro? Come on. Leo!

443
00:34:09.115 --> 00:34:11.208
- You all right?
- No prob.

444
00:34:19.706 --> 00:34:22.800
Power! Yeah.

445
00:34:25.722 --> 00:34:28.156
Oh. yeah!

446
00:34:30.169 --> 00:34:32.763
Look. I don't believe this.

447
00:34:34.649 --> 00:34:38.176
- Yes!
- Yes. yes!

448
00:34:40.985 --> 00:34:43.385
it's like spider city!

449
00:34:43.353 --> 00:34:45.446
Great!

450
00:34:45.433 --> 00:34:48.197
Rock-a-bye-baby.

451
00:34:48.152 --> 00:34:50.086
it's roomy!

452
00:34:50.072 --> 00:34:52.563
And it's well hidden. huh?

453
00:34:52.536 --> 00:34:54.527
So what do ya think?

454
00:34:55.992 --> 00:35:00.088
You know. i hear the sewers
in Connecticut are really nice.

455
00:34:59.992 --> 00:35:02.290
- Yeah. Come on.
- This is great!

456
00:35:07.832 --> 00:35:11.996
- How much longer?
- Look. i told you. i don't know.

457
00:35:11.895 --> 00:35:14.022
it takes time. Days!

458
00:35:14.007 --> 00:35:17.033
i want them
as soon as possible.

459
00:35:16.984 --> 00:35:19.976
- I told...
- Sit down!

460
00:35:19.927 --> 00:35:22.987
Aren't these enough
for your vengeance?

461
00:35:22.935 --> 00:35:26.166
The Foot have already
failed against them.

462
00:35:26.103 --> 00:35:28.367
i have failed.

463
00:35:30.167 --> 00:35:34.331
But the next time
will be different.

464
00:35:34.230 --> 00:35:38.860
The next fight will be
freak against freak!

465
00:35:43.126 --> 00:35:46.823
April. will you listen
just for a minute?

466
00:35:46.742 --> 00:35:48.676
it's a ratings week!

467
00:35:48.662 --> 00:35:52.120
Phil. i told you.
i am following up on TGRi.

468
00:35:52.053 --> 00:35:54.453
There's more going on there
than we know.

469
00:35:54.422 --> 00:35:58.051
Look. that story is over.
We need something solid.

470
00:35:57.973 --> 00:36:02.376
Something fresh.
i mean. like... like this.

471
00:36:02.261 --> 00:36:05.526
- She's busy right now.
- "Looking ahead.

472
00:36:05.461 --> 00:36:07.929
- Swimsuits in the '90s"?
- My interest is peaked.

473
00:36:07.893 --> 00:36:10.794
Phil. i gotta get going.

474
00:36:10.741 --> 00:36:12.800
You are always so busy.

475
00:36:12.789 --> 00:36:15.622
i'm the news manager here. April!

476
00:36:15.573 --> 00:36:18.474
April. there's a call for you.

477
00:36:19.764 --> 00:36:21.629
Tell them i'll call them back.

478
00:36:21.620 --> 00:36:25.112
He sounds pretty insistent.
Says his name's Donny.

479
00:36:25.044 --> 00:36:28.741
Listen. tell Donny that she's busy
with her news manager right now...

480
00:36:28.660 --> 00:36:30.218
and that she can't...

481
00:36:34.132 --> 00:36:37.499
Where are you guys?
Did you find a place to live yet?

482
00:36:37.427 --> 00:36:39.691
Oh. yeah. but i...

483
00:36:40.819 --> 00:36:43.754
it's not much right now.
but we'll bring you down.

484
00:36:43.699 --> 00:36:45.792
We've only really
had time to get Splinter...

485
00:36:45.779 --> 00:36:47.804
- And pick up a few essentials.
- Yeah!

486
00:36:47.795 --> 00:36:50.263
The bare essentials!

487
00:36:50.227 --> 00:36:53.287
Look. the reason why
we're calling is...

488
00:36:53.234 --> 00:36:56.169
have you seen Raphael
by any chance?

489
00:36:56.114 --> 00:36:58.048
Yeah. Has he stopped by
or anything?

490
00:36:58.034 --> 00:37:01.561
No. Why? Is he missing?

491
00:37:01.490 --> 00:37:06.052
You know. there's still more stuff
to help with. Michaelangelo!

492
00:37:05.938 --> 00:37:08.406
Hey. i'm helping Donny!
Give me the phone.

493
00:37:08.370 --> 00:37:10.930
Hey. give me that...

494
00:37:10.898 --> 00:37:14.163
- So you haven't seen him at all?
- No. I haven't.

495
00:37:14.098 --> 00:37:17.397
if she does. tell him thanks
for wasting our time!

496
00:37:17.330 --> 00:37:19.628
'Cause instead of looking
for the Foot and the ooze...

497
00:37:19.602 --> 00:37:21.536
like we should...

498
00:37:21.522 --> 00:37:25.424
we gotta go out and look
for him instead.

499
00:37:25.329 --> 00:37:30.767
- What was that?
- Leo says hi.

500
00:37:30.609 --> 00:37:32.577
- Donny. give me the phone.
- If you do hear something...

501
00:37:32.561 --> 00:37:35.894
- Let us know.
- I wanna talk to April! It's important!

502
00:37:35.824 --> 00:37:38.019
- Gimme. gimme. gimme!
- All right. here.

503
00:37:38.000 --> 00:37:41.265
April. it's Mikey.
i'd just like to say...

504
00:37:41.201 --> 00:37:44.227
- Hello.
- Would you give me that!

505
00:37:49.840 --> 00:37:52.570
The cells will
no longer hold them.

506
00:37:53.616 --> 00:37:56.414
Remove the bar.

507
00:37:56.368 --> 00:37:58.962
it's time they learn
who their master is.

508
00:38:00.720 --> 00:38:04.212
Remove the bar
and leave us.

509
00:38:11.536 --> 00:38:13.936
Come forth!

510
00:38:23.374 --> 00:38:28.107
Wolf. Snapping turtle.
incredible!

511
00:38:28.559 --> 00:38:30.754
Yes. Come forward.

512
00:38:30.735 --> 00:38:33.533
Attack me. if you will.

513
00:38:33.486 --> 00:38:36.978
When it is over.
you will call me "Master"!

514
00:38:45.998 --> 00:38:49.559
- Mama? Oh. Mama!
- Oh. Mama!

515
00:38:51.502 --> 00:38:54.960
- Mama.
- Mama.

516
00:38:54.894 --> 00:38:57.158
Get off me!

517
00:38:58.989 --> 00:39:01.184
Babies!

518
00:39:01.165 --> 00:39:03.895
They are babies!

519
00:39:06.413 --> 00:39:09.541
What did you expect?
They'd come out quoting Macbeth?

520
00:39:09.485 --> 00:39:13.421
- They are stupid!
- They're not stupid. They're infants.

521
00:39:16.812 --> 00:39:18.643
Okay. they're stupid infants.

522
00:39:21.516 --> 00:39:23.711
Put that down!

523
00:39:25.708 --> 00:39:29.974
Fortunately. they seem to have
imprinted you as their surrogate mother.

524
00:39:29.867 --> 00:39:33.735
- Mama.
- They are of no use to me against a...

525
00:39:35.499 --> 00:39:37.592
See that these two things...

526
00:39:37.580 --> 00:39:40.811
are properly disposed of.

527
00:39:40.747 --> 00:39:42.738
No. You can't do that.
They're living creatures.

528
00:39:43.979 --> 00:39:45.913
Not for long.

529
00:39:45.899 --> 00:39:49.130
Hey. no. no.
Wait. look.

530
00:39:50.443 --> 00:39:54.675
They may be
intellectually inferior. but...

531
00:39:58.603 --> 00:40:02.369
As you can see. they do have
other attributes.

532
00:40:05.802 --> 00:40:09.636
Maybe i'll keep them
around after all.

533
00:40:18.921 --> 00:40:21.549
- Hey. man. how's it going?
- Pretty good.

534
00:40:21.513 --> 00:40:23.674
- Good to see you. man.
- What's up?

535
00:40:23.657 --> 00:40:25.591
Did you just get here?

536
00:40:26.696 --> 00:40:28.926
Okay. guys.

537
00:40:28.905 --> 00:40:31.169
Listen up.

538
00:40:31.144 --> 00:40:33.874
i'm only going
to tell youse once.

539
00:40:33.832 --> 00:40:38.360
All of youse guys is gonna
have to take a little test.

540
00:40:38.249 --> 00:40:41.514
Then. if you're good enough...

541
00:40:41.449 --> 00:40:44.976
we let you into
the organization.

542
00:40:44.904 --> 00:40:48.305
Any questions?

543
00:40:48.232 --> 00:40:49.756
Okay. follow me.

544
00:40:49.768 --> 00:40:51.963
- Let's go.
- Lead the way. man.

545
00:41:02.760 --> 00:41:04.352
i knew this would work.

546
00:41:04.359 --> 00:41:08.056
just remember. we get you in.
we find the Foot headquarters...

547
00:41:07.975 --> 00:41:10.500
we get you out to tell
the others. right?

548
00:41:10.471 --> 00:41:13.065
Gee. maybe i should
write this down.

549
00:41:13.030 --> 00:41:15.157
What?

550
00:41:15.143 --> 00:41:17.304
i'm being punished. aren't i?

551
00:42:02.437 --> 00:42:04.769
- Keno. wasn't it?
- Yeah.

552
00:42:04.740 --> 00:42:07.470
You seem to be the only one
worthy of a final test.

553
00:42:09.476 --> 00:42:12.843
You'll have 15 seconds to remove
as many of the bells as you can.

554
00:42:13.604 --> 00:42:15.538
One sound and you fail.

555
00:42:15.524 --> 00:42:18.891
And another thing.
we work in concealment.

556
00:42:18.819 --> 00:42:20.787
Fifteen seconds.

557
00:42:20.772 --> 00:42:22.000
Go!

558
00:42:38.403 --> 00:42:39.529
is this enough?

559
00:42:42.083 --> 00:42:44.381
Yeah!

560
00:42:47.170 --> 00:42:49.104
Welcome to our headquarters.

561
00:42:50.914 --> 00:42:53.940
Get yourself a training dogi
and meet me back in the yard.

562
00:42:53.890 --> 00:42:55.414
Yeah. right.

563
00:43:05.601 --> 00:43:07.068
Keno. come on.

564
00:43:10.849 --> 00:43:13.841
Okay. Looks like
this is the place.

565
00:43:13.793 --> 00:43:15.727
Yeah. looks like it.

566
00:43:19.777 --> 00:43:22.974
First chance we get.
we're out of here.

567
00:43:22.913 --> 00:43:25.006
What? What is it?

568
00:43:27.072 --> 00:43:29.199
i thought i just saw a ghost.

569
00:43:30.656 --> 00:43:31.918
Come on.

570
00:43:32.769 --> 00:43:36.398
- What are we looking for anyway?
- Quiet. You want to get us...

571
00:43:38.464 --> 00:43:40.022
caught?

572
00:43:40.032 --> 00:43:41.056
Yeah. well...

573
00:43:42.431 --> 00:43:46.595
Hi. We were lookin' for
a muffler for a '77 Chevy.

574
00:43:49.440 --> 00:43:52.170
Whatever happened
to service with a smile?

575
00:43:54.496 --> 00:43:55.656
Yeah!

576
00:44:00.319 --> 00:44:04.119
Get out of here kid.
Go tell the others. Go now!

577
00:44:04.031 --> 00:44:06.499
Hey. nice shot.

578
00:44:06.463 --> 00:44:08.397
You're good.
Come on.

579
00:44:11.134 --> 00:44:13.659
- I'm not gonna just...
- Run. or i'll kick your butt.

580
00:44:17.662 --> 00:44:20.187
Move!
Come on. you guys!

581
00:44:27.038 --> 00:44:29.871
Excuse me.
Pardon me.

582
00:44:32.638 --> 00:44:35.334
Come on.

583
00:44:35.293 --> 00:44:36.658
Missed.

584
00:44:38.589 --> 00:44:40.523
i'm curious.

585
00:44:40.509 --> 00:44:44.775
Any of you guys ever heard
the expression "fair fight"?

586
00:44:47.005 --> 00:44:49.565
You know. pal.
if i had a face like yours...

587
00:44:49.532 --> 00:44:52.968
i'd try to make up for it
with some sort of a personality.

588
00:45:11.355 --> 00:45:15.792
Come on.
Come on. April. Leo!

589
00:45:15.676 --> 00:45:17.837
if you're there.
it's me. Keno.

590
00:45:17.819 --> 00:45:21.915
Darn. Come on.
Raph's in trouble.

591
00:45:24.571 --> 00:45:26.266
April. where are they?

592
00:45:26.267 --> 00:45:28.963
- It's Raph.
- Wait. calm down. What happened?

593
00:45:28.923 --> 00:45:31.084
i've gotta tell the guys.
They got him!

594
00:45:31.067 --> 00:45:33.001
Who has got him?

595
00:45:42.682 --> 00:45:44.616
Come on.

596
00:45:45.562 --> 00:45:48.463
- Just like Keno said.
- Yeah.

597
00:45:48.410 --> 00:45:50.674
- The perimeter's quiet.
- Yeah.

598
00:45:50.650 --> 00:45:53.278
A little too quiet.

599
00:45:53.241 --> 00:45:55.869
- Come on.
- Okay.

600
00:46:08.121 --> 00:46:09.679
Knock. knock.

601
00:46:13.305 --> 00:46:16.706
- Well. that was easy.
- Yeah. a little too easy.

602
00:46:22.200 --> 00:46:24.634
Look. it's Raph!

603
00:46:24.601 --> 00:46:26.831
Yeah. a little too Raph.

604
00:46:26.808 --> 00:46:30.574
You guys. knock it off.
Keep your eyes peeled.

605
00:46:30.488 --> 00:46:32.513
i don't like this.

606
00:46:32.504 --> 00:46:33.732
- Let's go.
- Right.

607
00:46:46.647 --> 00:46:49.309
You know. given the layout
of this junkyard...

608
00:46:49.271 --> 00:46:51.364
and the proximity
of certain structures...

609
00:46:51.351 --> 00:46:53.319
if they were gonna
spring a trap...

610
00:46:53.303 --> 00:46:56.363
they'd probably do it
right about...

611
00:47:00.182 --> 00:47:02.275
Let us out of here!

612
00:47:02.262 --> 00:47:04.093
What the...

613
00:47:08.503 --> 00:47:11.097
The Shred dude!
it's him!

614
00:47:11.062 --> 00:47:14.498
i've been waiting for you.

615
00:47:14.422 --> 00:47:17.186
i have a little surprise.

616
00:47:18.582 --> 00:47:23.178
- Oh. no.
- I don't like this.

617
00:47:23.062 --> 00:47:24.996
i wonder what those are for.

618
00:47:24.982 --> 00:47:27.974
Does the word "turtle-kabob"
mean anything to you?

619
00:47:27.925 --> 00:47:31.554
Yeah. right!
Get your arm out of my face.

620
00:47:34.613 --> 00:47:38.071
Patience.
First them...

621
00:47:38.005 --> 00:47:41.532
then you.

622
00:47:41.460 --> 00:47:44.452
You know. these nets
are remarkably effective.

623
00:47:44.405 --> 00:47:46.339
Very well constructed.

624
00:47:46.324 --> 00:47:49.487
Remind me to drop a line
to Ralph Nader!

625
00:47:49.429 --> 00:47:52.887
Wait for my signal
to drop them.

626
00:47:55.349 --> 00:47:57.317
i never got to see Paris.

627
00:47:57.300 --> 00:48:00.292
A little closer.

628
00:48:00.244 --> 00:48:02.576
A little closer!

629
00:48:02.548 --> 00:48:05.108
Oh. we're almost there!

630
00:48:06.548 --> 00:48:08.038
Get ready!

631
00:48:14.579 --> 00:48:17.673
Cowabunga!

632
00:48:17.619 --> 00:48:20.144
That's right. Shredder.
You forgot.

633
00:48:20.115 --> 00:48:24.245
- We carry insurance.
- Mutual of Splinter. dude.

634
00:48:24.147 --> 00:48:26.206
Get them!

635
00:48:39.986 --> 00:48:42.181
Why don't you just
rip my lips off?

636
00:48:42.162 --> 00:48:45.131
- You'd think...
- Enough.

637
00:48:45.073 --> 00:48:47.234
Here. let me get this first.

638
00:48:58.897 --> 00:49:01.457
Can we talk?

639
00:49:01.425 --> 00:49:02.722
Guess not!

640
00:49:05.009 --> 00:49:07.170
Pitiful.

641
00:49:15.600 --> 00:49:16.760
You win.

642
00:49:20.048 --> 00:49:22.881
- Looks like we're on our own.
- All right!

643
00:49:22.832 --> 00:49:24.959
Tokka!

644
00:49:24.944 --> 00:49:27.242
Rahzar!

645
00:49:38.160 --> 00:49:40.458
Didn't we see these guys
on Wrestlemania?

646
00:49:40.432 --> 00:49:44.266
Prove yourselves to me!
Attack!

647
00:49:46.255 --> 00:49:48.621
Well. you know
what they say.

648
00:49:48.591 --> 00:49:50.525
The bigger they are...

649
00:49:53.967 --> 00:49:55.594
The more bones
they break.

650
00:49:58.990 --> 00:50:02.084
- These guys are mine.
- Go get 'em. Donny.

651
00:50:02.030 --> 00:50:05.796
All right. you overgrown.
ugly excuse for a turtle!

652
00:50:11.469 --> 00:50:16.065
You know. maybe that "ugly" crack
was a little bit out of line.

653
00:50:24.077 --> 00:50:26.568
Oh. that hurt!

654
00:50:29.197 --> 00:50:31.791
Hey. you're that TGRi guy.

655
00:50:31.757 --> 00:50:33.691
Hang on.

656
00:50:35.724 --> 00:50:40.161
- I've got to get the hang of that.
- It's okay.

657
00:50:40.045 --> 00:50:42.639
i'm gonna get you
out of here.

658
00:50:58.636 --> 00:50:59.796
What?

659
00:51:01.995 --> 00:51:04.190
Oh. am i glad to see you!

660
00:51:06.732 --> 00:51:10.793
- Hey. guys. over here!
- Yeah! We're on our way.

661
00:51:12.139 --> 00:51:15.540
Come on. Professor.
We don't have a lot of time.

662
00:51:15.467 --> 00:51:20.234
- Hey. Mikey. we got the TGRi guy.
- Come on. come on.

663
00:51:20.107 --> 00:51:23.565
- Well. actually. i'd rather not.
- Come on!

664
00:51:25.226 --> 00:51:27.888
Step up to the bar. boys!

665
00:51:31.530 --> 00:51:33.464
This way. Leo.
Come on.

666
00:51:34.250 --> 00:51:35.808
You all right. Doc?

667
00:51:35.818 --> 00:51:39.117
- Way to go. Mikey!
- Come on. You go next.

668
00:51:39.050 --> 00:51:40.540
Come here.

669
00:51:41.578 --> 00:51:43.876
- Come on. Raph.
- Yeah. yeah.

670
00:51:45.353 --> 00:51:46.547
Stop them!

671
00:51:51.209 --> 00:51:54.576
- Drop right in. Leo.
- All right!

672
00:52:07.305 --> 00:52:10.297
Hey. look at this!

673
00:52:19.943 --> 00:52:21.001
Stupid!

674
00:52:23.304 --> 00:52:26.068
Come on. We gotta
meet back up with Splinter.

675
00:52:26.023 --> 00:52:27.615
Yeah.

676
00:52:30.407 --> 00:52:33.706
Four walking. talking turtles!

677
00:52:36.359 --> 00:52:39.556
Yeah. the guy's Ph.D. material.
all right.

678
00:52:39.495 --> 00:52:42.430
You're so intelligent.
it's incredible.

679
00:52:42.375 --> 00:52:45.902
Don't freak. dude.
We can explain. You see...

680
00:52:45.831 --> 00:52:47.958
Fifteen years ago.
you came into contact...

681
00:52:47.942 --> 00:52:50.240
with a green colloidal gel
down in a sewer...

682
00:52:50.214 --> 00:52:53.741
which transformed you
into your present state.

683
00:52:54.662 --> 00:52:56.129
Fantastic!

684
00:52:56.646 --> 00:52:59.547
There you go.
Come on. Yeah.

685
00:52:59.494 --> 00:53:01.052
Amazing. guys.

686
00:53:01.062 --> 00:53:04.725
i thought all the really
good dungeons were in Europe.

687
00:53:04.646 --> 00:53:06.443
There you go. dude.

688
00:53:09.477 --> 00:53:12.173
- This is wonderful!
- Yeah. okay.

689
00:53:12.134 --> 00:53:16.230
We'll give you the tour later.
Right now we've got a few questions.

690
00:53:16.133 --> 00:53:20.661
- A few inquiries.
- Yeah. a few...

691
00:53:20.549 --> 00:53:24.076
- We'll give you a tour later.
- Give him room to speak.

692
00:53:26.213 --> 00:53:29.341
The professor has much
to tell us.

693
00:53:36.740 --> 00:53:38.799
Of course. laboratories
were crude back then...

694
00:53:38.788 --> 00:53:41.916
and an accident was
just waiting to happen.

695
00:53:41.860 --> 00:53:45.387
Wait a minute.
You mean to tell us...

696
00:53:45.316 --> 00:53:49.150
that the formation of the ooze
was all just a big mistake?

697
00:53:49.060 --> 00:53:51.119
Let me see.

698
00:53:51.107 --> 00:53:53.769
Donatello. isn't it?

699
00:53:53.731 --> 00:53:56.393
An unknown mixture
of discarded chemicals...

700
00:53:56.355 --> 00:54:00.189
was accidentally exposed
to a series of radiated waves...

701
00:54:00.099 --> 00:54:03.535
and the resulting ooze
was found to have remarkable...

702
00:54:03.459 --> 00:54:07.054
but dangerous
mutanagenic properties.

703
00:54:08.739 --> 00:54:10.104
Big mistake.

704
00:54:14.307 --> 00:54:17.743
- Please continue. Professor.
- Yeah.

705
00:54:17.666 --> 00:54:20.328
Well. on our way to bury them.
a near collision caused us...

706
00:54:20.291 --> 00:54:24.853
to lose one of the canisters
down a sewer 15 years ago.

707
00:54:24.738 --> 00:54:28.401
Professor Perry.
what's happening at TGRi now?

708
00:54:29.154 --> 00:54:31.145
i imagine they're trying
to remove any evidence...

709
00:54:31.138 --> 00:54:33.698
of the disposal process
and evacuate the premises...

710
00:54:33.666 --> 00:54:36.658
which is standard procedure
when a mishap occurs.

711
00:54:36.610 --> 00:54:42.173
And as we know. one or two
rather big mishaps have occurred.

712
00:54:42.017 --> 00:54:45.453
Yeah.
Tokka. Rahzar and the Shredder.

713
00:54:45.377 --> 00:54:48.813
And he's obsessed
with destroying you all.

714
00:54:48.736 --> 00:54:51.796
Yeah. we got that impression.
all right.

715
00:54:51.745 --> 00:54:53.178
- Michaelangelo.
- Yeah?

716
00:54:53.184 --> 00:54:55.652
- Show the professor where he may rest.
- Righty-o!

717
00:54:56.545 --> 00:54:58.342
This way. dude.

718
00:54:58.336 --> 00:55:00.304
it ain't the Hilton.

719
00:55:02.464 --> 00:55:05.695
Let's face it. You'd be better off
staying at the Hilton.

720
00:55:12.800 --> 00:55:16.998
What troubles you. my son?

721
00:55:16.895 --> 00:55:21.195
i don't know. I just always thought
there'd be more to it...

722
00:55:21.087 --> 00:55:23.112
to the ooze...

723
00:55:23.103 --> 00:55:26.402
to. you know. us!

724
00:55:26.335 --> 00:55:28.394
i know.

725
00:55:28.383 --> 00:55:32.752
i always thought
there'd be something.

726
00:55:32.639 --> 00:55:35.369
i thought we'd find out
we were special.

727
00:55:35.326 --> 00:55:39.558
Do not confuse the specter
of your origin...

728
00:55:39.455 --> 00:55:41.855
with your present worth.
my sons.

729
00:55:41.823 --> 00:55:46.283
i don't believe him!
There's just got to be more to it!

730
00:55:46.175 --> 00:55:48.973
Perhaps the search
for a beginning...

731
00:55:48.926 --> 00:55:52.987
rarely has so easy an end.

732
00:55:52.894 --> 00:55:56.125
But our search
will have to wait.

733
00:55:56.062 --> 00:56:00.021
Tonight's encounter
has left us with...

734
00:55:59.933 --> 00:56:02.493
larger problems.

735
00:56:06.397 --> 00:56:07.329
i got 'em.

736
00:56:15.389 --> 00:56:19.382
Go. Play. Have fun.

737
00:56:19.293 --> 00:56:21.227
Fun!

738
00:56:24.636 --> 00:56:28.367
Tonight we leave a calling card
for the turtles.

739
00:56:28.284 --> 00:56:33.187
Tomorrow we force
a final confrontation.

740
00:56:58.330 --> 00:57:02.130
- Master say have fun!
- Fun!

741
00:57:03.611 --> 00:57:05.545
Look. Sophie.

742
00:57:05.531 --> 00:57:08.091
Some animals are knocking down
the telephone poles.

743
00:57:08.059 --> 00:57:10.220
What do we do
if they come over here?

744
00:57:10.203 --> 00:57:12.763
Let them get
their own cab.

745
00:57:24.570 --> 00:57:26.504
Damage is minimal.

746
00:57:26.489 --> 00:57:29.925
And as always. our official report
will be released...

747
00:57:29.850 --> 00:57:31.784
after a thorough investigation.

748
00:57:31.770 --> 00:57:33.704
Thank you. Miss O'Neil.

749
00:57:33.690 --> 00:57:36.625
i have no further comments
at this time.

750
00:57:36.569 --> 00:57:38.503
We will be in touch.

751
00:57:38.489 --> 00:57:41.947
More as it develops.
Here you go.

752
00:57:41.881 --> 00:57:44.850
Chief Sterns. i wonder
if i might ask you...

753
00:57:44.793 --> 00:57:47.023
a few more questions
